<title>ESTONIA: GDP GREW 4 PCT IN 1996.</title>
<headline>GDP GREW 4 PCT IN 1996.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonia's gross domestic</p>
<p>product (GDP) grew by four percent in 1996 and by 7.3 percent in</p>
<p>the fourth quarter of 1996, the statistics office said Tuesday.</p>
<p>GDP grew 4.3 percent in 1995 and by 4.5 percent in the third</p>
<p>quarter of 1996, the office added in a statement.</p>
<p>GDP in current prices was 52.4 billion kroons in 1996 and</p>
<p>14.5 billion kroons in the fourth quarter. </p>
<p>Growth was biggest in the non-financial corporations sector</p>
<p>and the financial sector.</p>
<p>GDP in constant prices fell in the government sector,</p>
<p>because of the decreasing number of medical workers in state</p>
<p>budget institutions.</p>
<p>GDP by field of activity in 1993 constant prices in</p>
<p>millions of kroons in major economic areas:</p>
<p>			1995		1996	  change, pct</p>
<p>Agriculture</p>
<p>and hunting     1,564.9	   1,499.0	   -4.2</p>
<p>Forestry	    325.6	     359.4	   10.4</p>
<p>Fishing	     136.7	     164.7	   20.5</p>
<p>Construction    1,323.5	   1,454.7	    9.9</p>
<p>Transport,</p>
<p>communication   2,405.4	   2,738.1	   13.8</p>
<p>Financial</p>
<p>intermediation,</p>
<p>banking and</p>
<p>insurance	   596.1	     644.3	    8.1</p>
<p>Manufacturing   3,812.6	   3,819.4	    0.2</p>
<p>Wholesale and</p>
<p>retail trade    3,750.3	   3,959.8	    5.6</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400,</p>
<p>reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
